# The bus walk takes the first keyboard it finds, and the root-port one
# comes before the hub on port 4. Unplug it so the hub is the only route
# to a keyboard, and this test drives the hub path rather than repeating
# what usb-kbd-connect already covers.
#
# -hid-keys plus a held make scancode in the .keys sidecar, because under the
# NAK model (default since main 13889) an interrupt endpoint completes only
# when the report differs from the last delivered one, and an untyped keyboard
# reports zeros forever. With the root keyboard unplugged the HUB keyboard is
# the one that carries the keys (hid_kbd_carries_keys, codex-vm.c:1167), which
# is the endpoint this test is about.
-xhci-no-root-kbd -hid-keys
